From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: j7prime p3 <p3@j7prime.invalid>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 01:00:00 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: exynos7870: add the ISP power domain

Describe the ISP power domain (PMU 0x4040) and put CMU_ISP in it, so the
domain stays off until something needs its clocks.

To skip on a test boot: pd_ignore_unused on the command line keeps every
unused power domain on (genpd).

Origin: Martin Štrobl, github.com/a3y17lte-mainline/kernel_samsung_exynos7870 (branch lineage-24.0) commit 5208351dde6f.
---

Notes:
    Port to v7.3.4 + j7prime 0001-0017: power domain node and power-domains property only; the
    assigned-clocks part (MIF CAM inputs to the lowest vendor level) is left out because our
    clock binding header has no ID for ffac_mif_mux_media_pll_div2 (needs a binding change first).

 arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/exynos7870.dtsi | 9 +++++++++
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+), 0 deletions(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/exynos7870.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/exynos7870.dtsi
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/exynos7870.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/exynos7870.dtsi
@@ -297,6 +297,14 @@
 			};
 		};
 
+		pd_isp: power-domain@10484040 {
+			compatible = "samsung,exynos7870-pd",
+				     "samsung,exynos5433-pd";
+			reg = <0x10484040 0x20>;
+			#power-domain-cells = <0>;
+			label = "isp";
+		};
+
 		gic: interrupt-controller@104e1000 {
 			compatible = "arm,cortex-a15-gic";
 			reg = <0x104e1000 0x1000>,
@@ -830,6 +838,7 @@
 				 <&cmu_mif CLK_GOUT_MIF_CMU_ISP_CAM>,
 				 <&cmu_mif CLK_GOUT_MIF_CMU_ISP_ISP>,
 				 <&cmu_mif CLK_GOUT_MIF_CMU_ISP_VRA>;
+			power-domains = <&pd_isp>;
 		};
 
 		syscon_cam0: system-controller@144f1040 {
-- 
